Additionally, this will help us to see whether the x is added to the correct position or not. If it is added and the previous and following positions are null for the x, then it is correctly implemented. 

In the scenario where 'index > Old_arrListCount', the new index would be inserted at the end of the list. The code to verify this should be:
```cs
            Debug.Assert(New_arrListCount == Old_arrListCount + 1 || New_arrListCount == index);
